      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Crowley are proud to bring to the market a truly unique property. St Catherine's is a former Church of Ireland church built circa 1800 and converted in 2006 into a substantial family home of immense character.\n\nThe property was retired from use as a church circa 1990 and its conversion was architecturally overseen to an exceptional standard. Built of limestone, the property successfully blends the old and new to create a comfortable and atmospheric residence. Some of St Catherine's exceptional features include Egyptian sandstone flagstone tiling throughout the ground floor, an original stained glass window in the kitchen/ dining room which was sensitively restored by local artist Linda Grieve/Mulloy and some of the original flagstone flooring. \n\nThe floor area measures approximately 432.9 sq m/4,660 sq ft over three stories. Ground floor accommodation comprises of entrance hall, living room, sitting room, substantial kitchen/dining room with raised dining area and overhead dome, utility, office/study and shower room. On the first floor there is a large library/sitting room, seven bedrooms (three en-suite) and a family bathroom. Bedrooms 2 and 3 are both single rooms which could easily be converted to one larger bedroom. On the third floor there is a very substantial master bedroom suite with walk-in wardrobe and en-suite. There is also an additional substantial room which could suit as an office or workroom. \n\nThe secluded gardens are surrounded by stone walls and mature trees and shrubs. A paved courtyard to the side and a rear patio have been created using some of the original flagstones from the church. The is also a small lawn area, a gravel driveway providing ample parking and stone sheds (9.0m x 3.75m).\n\nThe property's entrance driveway is shared with a small graveyard with access provided to those visiting/caretaking family graves. \n\nThe property is located in the centre of Newport town accessed from Main Street by Church Lane. Newport is an attractive small town set on the Newport River at the mouth of Clew Bay. The town's amenities include primary school, shops, restaurants, bars and hotel. It has many leisure facilities on its doorstep including Newport Harbour and the Great Western Greenway walking/cycling trail which runs from Westport to Achill Island. Westport town is a 10 minute drive and Ireland West International Airport is a 55 minute drive."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 8.05m x 1.47m & 3.3m x 1.83m & 4.4m x 2.1m\nEgyptian sandstone tiled floor, open tread staircase\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 7.2m x 6.6m & 5.1m x 3.1m\nOak floor, feature stained glass window, raised dining area (original pulpit area) with some original timbers used to construct the steps, solid oak kitchen with tiled and brick back splashes, walk-in pantry, hand crafted sold oak open tread staircase (requires banisters), double doors on either side of room to the garden\n\nLiving Room - 5.67m x 4.7m\nEgyptian sandstone tiled floor, marble fireplace with solid fuel stove, cornicing, doors to garden, curtains\n\nSitting Room - 4.8m x 3.7m\nEgyptian sandstone tiled floor, cornicing, electric fire, patio doors to side garden\n\nOffice/Study - 3.05m x 2.2m\nEgyptian sandstone tiled floor\n\nUtility Room - 2.9m x 2.2m\nEgyptian sandstone tiled floor, sink unit\n\nBack Hallway - 3.9m x 2.6m\nOriginal flagstone floor, exposed stone wall\n\nShower Room - 2.4m x 2.2m\nFully tiled wetroom, shower, wc, whb\n\nBack Porch/Plant Room - 2.5m x 1.69m\nOriginal arched doorway to back garden, internal door frames/fanlight windows and flagstone floor, oil boiler, water tank\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 15.6m x 1.17m\nFrench pine floor, open tread staircase to second floor\n\nLibrary/Study - 3.36m x 3.38m & 2.34m x 2.0m\nFeature gothic circular window, French pine floor\n\nBedroom One - 3.18m x 2.58m\nFrench pine floor, pointed arch window, curtains\n\nEn-Suite - 2.75m x 2.2m\nFully tiled, arched window, shower, wc, whb\n\nBedroom Two - 3.28m x 2.3m\nFrench pine floor, single bedroom\n\nBedroom Three - 3.28m x 2.6m\nFrench pine floor, single bedroom (could be opened into Bedroom Two to provide a large double bedroom)\n\nBedroom Four - 4.3m x 3.27m\nFrench pine floor, pointed arch window\n\nEn-Suite - 2.65m x 0.96m\nFully tiled, shower, wc, whb\n\nBedroom Five - 3.73m x 2.57m\nFrench pine floor, pointed arch window, curtains\n\nBedroom Six - 5.0m x 2.58m\n